# A port outside the change breaks, in the middle of a cohort that had
# already proven half of itself. oniguruma built and is passed on its
# own evidence; jq was reached, and what broke under it was pkgconfig,
# which this branch never touched.
#
# jq is blocked with the stranger named in its detail and nothing in
# its blamed field. Blamed names a SUBJECT — the sibling whose failure
# a member inherited — and a port outside the change is not one; a
# reader that found pkgconfig there would go looking for it among the
# change's own members and find nothing.
#
# This is the shape that shows plurality has a consequence the single
# case never had: the record now holds a pass and a block and no
# failure at all, which is Record.Promotable's "at least one passed and
# none failed". The promote gate is the schema's and this corpus only
# states what the settle wrote, but the combination is new and worth
# seeing here.
# SYNTHESIZED from the cohort runner in internal/verify/tart/tart.go,
# not captured: see README.md.
members: oniguruma jq
outcome: failed
oniguruma.state: passed
oniguruma.lint: clean
jq.state: blocked
jq.detail: dependency pkgconfig fails to build; the change itself is untested
